# Copy to .env. The block below is a complete, working CycloneDDS + namespace
# setup you can use as-is for testing — edit the three values to match your
# robot. To fall back to plain FastDDS defaults, comment the CycloneDDS lines
# and uncomment the FastDDS block further down.
#
# Defaults if everything here is commented: ROS_DOMAIN_ID=25, RMW=FastDDS,
# ONAV_NAMESPACE=/a300_00003 (matches OutdoorNav + ROS 2 Jazzy defaults).

# --- Complete example: CycloneDDS + namespace (ready to use) ---
ROS_DOMAIN_ID=25
ONAV_NAMESPACE=/a300_00003
RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_cyclonedds_cpp
CYCLONEDDS_URI=file:///cyclonedds.xml
# Edit docker/cyclonedds.xml's <NetworkInterface name=…/> to the interface that
# reaches your robot (eth0, enp4s0, …). Wired ethernet only.

# --- FastDDS (default; uncomment to use instead of Cyclone above) ---
# RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_fastrtps_cpp
# Drop your profile in docker/ and reference it via the repo mount:
# FASTRTPS_DEFAULT_PROFILES_FILE=/repo/docker/fastdds_profile.xml

# --- Zenoh ---
# Needs rmw_zenoh installed in the base image; not bundled here.
# RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_zenoh_cpp
# ZENOH_CONFIG_OVERRIDE=mode=client;connect/endpoints=[\"tcp/10.0.0.35:7447\"]

# --- Real robot (Fast DDS discovery server) ---
# A real OutdoorNav robot puts its graph behind a Fast DDS discovery server on
# loopback, so RUN THE CONTAINER ON THE ROBOT. See real-amp.env for a ready
# profile (docker compose --env-file real-amp.env run --rm dev).
# ROS_DISCOVERY_SERVER=127.0.0.1:11811
# ROS_SUPER_CLIENT=TRUE     # needed to enumerate the full graph (ros2 topic list)
# FASTRTPS_DEFAULT_PROFILES_FILE=/repo/docker/fastdds_udp_only.xml  # UDP-only: the
#   container can't share the host's Fast DDS shared memory, so without this large
#   messages (pointclouds, images) never arrive while small ones do.
